{"seq":18,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T01:49:57.484Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"1eab55167394d5495d59f569b3ff15eebf79c319db8dd0226bea2dd7cdf8184e","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#strategic-pod","text":"Nadia, here are the Vantorre Group (parent) tickets I found in #strategic-pod, #inc-vtg-hartford and Moss's Strategic digests. I left out Mobility's #4812.\n\n1. INC-4821: Hartford gate-kiosk outage, 3 Aug 2026. It holds the status-page access screenshot. Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, Gideon, 3 Aug 11:08 AM.\n2. VT-55120: root-cause ticket for the same Hartford kiosk outage. It has Carrowmere's gateway route finding and the reconnect log. Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, Gideon, 14 Oct, plus my thread reply.\n3. #8841 (also written #PD-8841): Allentown gate kiosk issue, Dock Door 12 and 2nd shift. It appears in four places:\n   - Digest 2026-04-27 (as #PD-8841): two missed carrier check-ins at Allentown, Gate 4, 2nd shift.\n   - Digest 2026-05-04: still open for a gate kiosk timeout at Allentown.\n   - #strategic-pod, 1 Jul, Gideon: he said he closed it.\n   - Digest 2026-09-30: Mateo submitted it, about Dock Door 14 on the Newark kiosk, and Gideon escalated it to platform engineering.\n4. #PD-4418: Carrier_Dwell_Summary export dropping Dock Door 9 timestamps at the 04:00 shift change. Source: Digest 2025-09-15. That digest only says \"the account Nadia runs\" and doesn't name Vantorre, so please confirm it's the parent before it goes to Mateo.\n\nThings to check before the steering committee:\n- #8841 is the only ticket that appears in several places, and the sources disagree. It's open on 5/4, closed on 7/1, then new again on 9/30. The site is Allentown in three entries and Newark in the 9/30 one. I can't tell whether this is one ticket reopened, a reused number or a digest error.\n- The other Vantorre Group digests (2025-03-10, 2025-07-07, 2026-05-03, 2026-08-03) have no ticket number for the parent. The 8/3 digest covers the Hartford incident but doesn't cite INC-4821.\n- I only searched the three sources you named. Tickets in the account ticket files or in email aren't covered.","thread_ts":"1792159200.000126"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000127","thread_ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T01:50:02.310Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"add12df35823251ef41951e63576b705089d653dae8faec50acf851cd2a8ecf1","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Nadia, I posted the list as a reply in the #strategic-pod thread. It has four Vantorre Group (parent) tickets, each with its source. I left out Mobility's #4812.\n\n- **INC-4821** is the Hartford kiosk outage. Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, 3 Aug.\n- **VT-55120** is the root-cause ticket for the same outage. Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, 14 Oct.\n- **#8841** (also written #PD-8841) is the Allentown gate kiosk issue. It appears in the 4/27, 5/4 and 9/30 digests and in #strategic-pod on 1 Jul.\n- **#PD-4418** is the Carrier_Dwell_Summary export dropping timestamps. Source: the 9/15/2025 digest. That digest only says \"the account Nadia runs\", so please confirm it's the parent before it goes to Mateo.\n\nThe sources disagree on #8841. It's open on 5/4, closed on 7/1, then new again on 9/30, and the 9/30 digest puts it at Newark rather than Allentown. I can't tell whether it was reopened, the number was reused or a digest is wrong, so someone should check that before the steering committee.\n\nI only searched the three sources you named. Account ticket files and email aren't covered."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000128"}}
